    "physical_description": "Sarong of cotton batik. The sarong is sewn into a tube with the kepala (front panel) of dark blue with brown and white tumpals, and with a dark blue Chinese influenced floral pattern. The main field is covered with a geometric design of dark red squares with blue centres arranged in a trellis pattern.  ",
    "summary": "This sarong is sewn into a tube with the <i>kepala</i> (front panel) in dark blue with brown and white tumpals and a dark blue Chinese influenced floral pattern. The main field is covered with a geometric design of dark red squares with blue centres arranged in a trellis pattern. There is a strong Indian incluence in the colours. \r\n\r\nThe sarong is associated with Jambi, southern Sumatra, and was almost certainly made there, although the suggestion has been made that such cloths were made in Java for export to Sumatra.",
